  "findings": "Compared wild-type pale cup-flower closeups and whole shrub, excluding named cultivar references. Dedicated smaller evergreen leaves and terminal white cups, with increased older foliage after sparse first pass. Current roughly 1.6-3.7 m family includes denser compact and open woodland forms. Fine pink markings and cup pockets are below 25 mm; pale existing palette retained. Actually reviewed final seeds 1,4,7 and all 36 variants after refactoring. Accepted stylized spring source; user endorsement remains separate.",
